  "limitations": [
    "Relaxation is at zero pressure. Deposited cells measured in a pressure cell are listed under measured_under_pressure and kept in the statistics.",
    "The reference is a measured cell, not a DFT cell. This is CHGNet's distance from experiment, not its error against the DFT-PBE data it was trained on.",
    "This measures geometry only. It says nothing about the energies anneal reports, which have no experimental counterpart here.",
    "A temperature bin is a population of structures, not a controlled variable. Bins differ in chemistry and cell size as well as temperature, so each bin reports its carbon-containing count and median site count beside its error.",
    "Zero-point motion expands a real crystal even at 0 K. CHGNet predicts a static lattice, so even the coldest bin is not a like-for-like comparison.",
    "A stress threshold leaves a residual volume strain of roughly threshold over bulk modulus: about 1% for a molecular crystal near 10 GPa at 0.1 GPa, and a few tenths of a percent for stiff inorganic solids.",
    "a, b and c are compared vector by vector in the deposited setting. For a large or strongly sheared deformation the volume error is the robust number.",
    "Runs that hit the step ceiling are under-relaxed, so their errors lean toward the deposited cell. They are reported separately.",
    "The sample comes from data/catalog.csv, a volume-bounded COD query already filtered for ordered sites, declared hydrogen and Z <= 94, cut here to 2-100 sites. The statistics describe that population, not COD as a whole.",
    "Hydrogen positions from X-ray refinement are poorly determined, and CHGNet moves them. Structures containing hydrogen are not separated out here."
  ]
